values ('ap_physics_2', 9, '9.4', array['9.4']::text[], 'formula', 'First law of thermodynamics', '\Delta U = Q + W', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The CED states the first law as conservation of energy for a closed system: the change in internal energy is the sum of energy transferred by heating (or cooling) and work done on the system. In \Delta U = Q + W, W is work done ON the system. Work done by the gas on its surroundings makes W negative. For an isolated system, the total energy is constant.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-2-reference-u9-u11-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_2-u9-r2-002; ced=9.4.B.1.ii: "the change in internal energy is the sum of energy transferred to or from the system by heating, or work done on the system"')
