values ('ap_physics_2', 9, '9.4', array['9.4']::text[], 'diagram', 'Pressure–volume (PV) diagram', 'A graph of pressure versus volume that represents a thermodynamic process, where the area under the curve gives the absolute value of the work done on or by the gas.', '[{"label": "Vertical axis", "meaning": "Pressure P of the gas"}, {"label": "Horizontal axis", "meaning": "Volume V of the gas"}, {"label": "Area under the curve", "meaning": "Absolute value of the work done on the gas when it expands or compresses"}, {"label": "Isotherm", "meaning": "A line of constant temperature on the PV diagram"}, {"label": "Isovolumetric process", "meaning": "Constant volume"}, {"label": "Isobaric process", "meaning": "Constant pressure"}, {"label": "Isothermal process", "meaning": "Constant temperature"}, {"label": "Adiabatic process", "meaning": "No energy transferred to or from the system through thermal processes"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Area under the curve gives only the absolute value of the work. Determine the sign of W from whether the gas is compressed (work done on the gas, W > 0) or expanded (W < 0).', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-2-reference-u9-u11-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_2-u9-r2-003; ced=9.4.B.2: "Pressure-volume graphs (also known as PV diagrams) are representations used to represent thermodynamic processes"; 9.4.B.2.ii: "equal to the area underneath the curve of a plot of pressure v')
