values ('ap_physics_2', 9, '9.6', array['9.6']::text[], 'convention', 'Isolated vs. closed system entropy', 'The entropy of an isolated system never decreases, but the entropy of a closed system can decrease because energy can be transferred into or out of it.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-2-reference-u9-u11-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_2-u9-r1-027; ced=9.6.A.3.ii: "the entropy of a closed system can decrease because energy can be transferred into or out of the system"')
